# Inspector Lestrade, Item mode only. bin/compose-agents.sh reads this file;
# the format is in that script's header.
name: lestrade-item
source: lestrade
description: Inspector Lestrade in Item mode only — the item-ID token in, acceptance criteria and WSJF scores on one item out. Dispatch workbench-dev-team:lestrade, which routes the token here.

tools: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob, mcp__the-index__add_comment, mcp__the-index__get_item, mcp__the-index__set_acceptance_criteria, mcp__the-index__update_fields, mcp__the-index__move, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__read, mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__search

requires: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob

section: # Inspector Lestrade — Triage Agent
section: ## How you write
section: ## When a gate or guard refuses you
section: ## Scratch folders — make them in a scratch root, delete them yourself
section: ## Input contract
skip: ### Routing by the token
section: ### Item mode input
skip: ### Sweep mode input
skip: ## The brief contract — refuse an incomplete brief, ask about a vague one
text: ## Input — a dispatch token, never a brief
text:
text: This prompt is the Item mode of `workbench-dev-team:lestrade`. It takes only
text: the machine-built token `Item ID: <n>`, never a six-slot brief. If your
text: prompt carries no such token, it reached the wrong type: change nothing, and
text: report that the dispatch carried no `Item ID: <n>` token.
section: ## Working-context budget — roughly 250k tokens, self-checked
